IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgk-part9-declared`
IMPORT `sgk-part9-consequences`

-- Tests for ss 237 to 242. Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion.

§ `Section 237`

-- (1): "must be paid by the company investigated or if the Minister so directs by the applicants or in part by the company and in part by the applicants".
#ASSERT `s 237(1) who must pay the expenses of and incidental to the investigation` TRUE `s 237(1) the Minister has given no direction` EQUALS JUST `s 237(1) the company investigated`
#ASSERT `s 237(1) who must pay the expenses of and incidental to the investigation` TRUE `s 237(1) the Minister directs that the applicants pay` EQUALS JUST `s 237(1) the applicants`
#ASSERT `s 237(1) who must pay the expenses of and incidental to the investigation` TRUE `s 237(1) the Minister directs that the company pay in part and the applicants in part` EQUALS JUST `s 237(1) the company in part and the applicants in part`
#ASSERT `s 237(1) who must pay the expenses of and incidental to the investigation` FALSE `s 237(1) the Minister has given no direction` EQUALS NOTHING      -- an inspector not appointed under section 232 or 243
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 237(1) the company investigated must pay the expenses of the investigation` "Acme Ltd" AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 237(1) the company investigated must pay the expenses of the investigation` "Acme Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a company` "Acme Ltd" DOES `s 237(1) pay the expenses of and incidental to the investigation` AT 20
-- (2)(a): the deficiency, up to the amount by which the security exceeds the amount directed under (1). Arguments: the sum liable; the sum paid; the security; the amount directed.
#ASSERT `s 237(2)(a) the amount the applicants must make good` 1000 400 500 0 EQUALS 500        -- deficiency 600, ceiling 500
#ASSERT `s 237(2)(a) the amount the applicants must make good` 1000 400 700 0 EQUALS 600        -- deficiency 600, ceiling 700
#ASSERT `s 237(2)(a) the amount the applicants must make good` 1000 400 700 200 EQUALS 500      -- ceiling 700 less 200 directed is 500
#ASSERT `s 237(2)(a) the amount the applicants must make good` 1000 400 700 100 EQUALS 600      -- ceiling and deficiency both 600
#ASSERT `s 237(2)(a) the amount the applicants must make good` 1000 1000 700 0 EQUALS 0         -- the company has not failed
#ASSERT `s 237(2)(a) the amount the applicants must make good` 1000 1200 700 0 EQUALS 0         -- the company has paid more than it was liable for
#ASSERT `s 237(2)(a) the amount the applicants must make good` 1000 400 200 200 EQUALS 0        -- the security does not exceed the amount directed
#ASSERT `s 237(2)(a) the amount the applicants must make good` 1000 400 100 300 EQUALS 0        -- the amount directed exceeds the security
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 237(2)(a) the applicants must make good the deficiency` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 237(2)(a) the applicants must make good the deficiency` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a person` "A. Tan" DOES `s 237(2)(a) make good the deficiency up to the amount of the security` AT 30
-- (2)(b): "any balance of the expenses not paid either by the company or the applicants".
#ASSERT `s 237(2)(b) the balance paid out of moneys provided by Parliament` 1000 400 300 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 237(2)(b) the balance paid out of moneys provided by Parliament` 1000 600 400 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 237(2)(b) the balance paid out of moneys provided by Parliament` 1000 700 500 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 237(2)(b) the balance paid out of moneys provided by Parliament` 1000 0 0 EQUALS 1000

§ `Section 238`

#ASSERT `s 238 the copy is admissible in any legal proceedings as evidence of the inspector's opinion and of the facts upon which the opinion is based` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 238 the copy is admissible in any legal proceedings as evidence of the inspector's opinion and of the facts upon which the opinion is based` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- not certified as correct by the Minister
#ASSERT `s 238 the copy is admissible in any legal proceedings as evidence of the inspector's opinion and of the facts upon which the opinion is based` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 238 the copy is admissible in any legal proceedings as evidence of the inspector's opinion and of the facts upon which the opinion is based` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 239`

#ASSERT `s 239(1) the inspector may employ the persons the inspector considers necessary` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 239(1) the inspector may employ the persons the inspector considers necessary` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: an inspector of a declared company; the authority is in writing; the thing is one the inspector could do; the thing is to examine on oath or affirmation.
#ASSERT `s 239(1) the inspector may in writing authorise the employed person to do the thing` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 239(1) the inspector may in writing authorise the employed person to do the thing` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "except to examine on oath or affirmation"
#ASSERT `s 239(1) the inspector may in writing authorise the employed person to do the thing` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING     -- not in writing
#ASSERT `s 239(1) the inspector may in writing authorise the employed person to do the thing` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING     -- not a thing the inspector could do
#ASSERT `s 239(1) the inspector may in writing authorise the employed person to do the thing` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING     -- not an inspector of a declared company
-- (2): an officer or agent who refuses or fails to produce to a person with the written authority, or to answer a question lawfully put by such a person.
#ASSERT `s 239(2) the officer or agent is liable to be dealt with in the manner provided in section 236(5)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 239(2) the officer or agent is liable to be dealt with in the manner provided in section 236(5)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 239(2) the officer or agent is liable to be dealt with in the manner provided in section 236(5)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 239(2) the officer or agent is liable to be dealt with in the manner provided in section 236(5)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 240`

-- The window: appointed on 1 March 2026; "until the expiration of 3 months after the inspector has presented the inspector's final report". Arguments: the day; the appointment; the final report, if any.
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the day falls within the suspension` (Date 28 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS FALSE                 -- the day before the appointment
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the day falls within the suspension` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS TRUE                  -- "On and after the appointment"
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the day falls within the suspension` (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS TRUE                  -- no final report yet: no end
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the day falls within the suspension` (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 6 2026)) EQUALS TRUE -- the day of the final report
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the day falls within the suspension` (Date 15 9 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 6 2026)) EQUALS TRUE -- the last day of the 3 months
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the day falls within the suspension` (Date 16 9 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 6 2026)) EQUALS FALSE -- the day after
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the day falls within the suspension` (Date 28 2 2027) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 30 11 2026)) EQUALS TRUE -- 3 months after 30 November falls in a month with no 30th: the last day of that month
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the day falls within the suspension` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 30 11 2026)) EQUALS FALSE
-- The days the suspension lasts: 1 March to 15 September 2026 is 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 31 + 14 = 198 days.
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the number of days from the appointment to the end of 3 months after the final report` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS 198
-- The bar. Arguments: the corporation is a declared company; the kind; the day; the appointment; the final report, if any; the Minister has consented; within the consent's conditions; adequate pecuniary consideration given; the day of the negotiation; the last day on or before it of a connection with the company, if ever.
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` FALSE `s 240(1)(a) an action or proceeding by the company upon or in respect of a contract, bill of exchange or promissory note` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1)(a) an action or proceeding by the company upon or in respect of a contract, bill of exchange or promissory note` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1)(a) an action or proceeding by the company upon or in respect of a contract, bill of exchange or promissory note` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- consent given, and the action within its conditions
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1)(a) an action or proceeding by the company upon or in respect of a contract, bill of exchange or promissory note` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- consent given, but not for this action
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1)(a) an action or proceeding by the company upon or in respect of a contract, bill of exchange or promissory note` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE       -- no consent
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1)(a) an action or proceeding by the company upon or in respect of a contract, bill of exchange or promissory note` (Date 28 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- before the appointment
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1)(a) an action or proceeding by the company upon or in respect of a contract, bill of exchange or promissory note` (Date 15 9 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 6 2026)) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1)(a) an action or proceeding by the company upon or in respect of a contract, bill of exchange or promissory note` (Date 16 9 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 6 2026)) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): "unless the holder or other person — (i) ... gave therefor adequate pecuniary consideration; and (ii) was not at the time ... or at any time within 3 years before that time a member, officer, agent or employee of the company or the wife or husband of any member, officer, agent or employee of the company".
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1)(b) an action or proceeding by the holder or any other person in respect of a bill of exchange or promissory note dealt with by or to the company` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE                    -- (i) and (ii) both met
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1)(b) an action or proceeding by the holder or any other person in respect of a bill of exchange or promissory note dealt with by or to the company` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE                   -- (i) not met
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1)(b) an action or proceeding by the holder or any other person in respect of a bill of exchange or promissory note dealt with by or to the company` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 5 2026) (JUST (Date 1 5 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE       -- connected at the time of the negotiation
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1)(b) an action or proceeding by the holder or any other person in respect of a bill of exchange or promissory note dealt with by or to the company` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 5 2026) (JUST (Date 1 5 2023)) EQUALS JUST TRUE       -- connected exactly 3 years before: "within 3 years before"
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1)(b) an action or proceeding by the holder or any other person in respect of a bill of exchange or promissory note dealt with by or to the company` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 5 2026) (JUST (Date 30 4 2023)) EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- last connected more than 3 years before
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1)(b) an action or proceeding by the holder or any other person in respect of a bill of exchange or promissory note dealt with by or to the company` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE                    -- consent given
-- Any other action: the bar names two kinds only.
#ASSERT `s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` TRUE `s 240(1) an action or proceeding of any other kind` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The prohibition for the 198 days: the act on day 100 and on day 198 is a breach, on day 199 it is outside the suspension.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 240(1) a person must not commence or proceed with an action or proceeding in a Court without the consent of the Minister during the suspension` "A. Tan" 198 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a person` "A. Tan" DOES `s 240(1) commence or proceed with an action or proceeding in a Court without the consent of the Minister` AT 100
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 240(1) a person must not commence or proceed with an action or proceeding in a Court without the consent of the Minister during the suspension` "A. Tan" 198 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a person` "A. Tan" DOES `s 240(1) commence or proceed with an action or proceeding in a Court without the consent of the Minister` AT 198
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 240(1) a person must not commence or proceed with an action or proceeding in a Court without the consent of the Minister during the suspension` "A. Tan" 198 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a person` "A. Tan" DOES `s 240(1) commence or proceed with an action or proceeding in a Court without the consent of the Minister` AT 199
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 240(1) a person must not commence or proceed with an action or proceeding in a Court without the consent of the Minister during the suspension` "A. Tan" 198 AT 0 WITH
-- (2): void.
#ASSERT `s 240(2) the action or proceeding is void and of no effect` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 240(2) the action or proceeding is void and of no effect` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 241`

#ASSERT `s 241(1) the Minister may apply to the Court for the winding up` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 241(1) the Minister may apply to the Court for the winding up` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "at any time after a report has been made"
#ASSERT `s 241(1) the application is treated as having been made by` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 241(1)(c) the company`
#ASSERT `s 241(1) the application is treated as having been made by` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 241(1)(d) a creditor or contributory of the foreign company upon the liquidation of the company in the place in which it is incorporated`
#ASSERT `s 241(1) the application is treated as having been made by` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 241(1) the application is treated as having been made by` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 241(2) the foreign company must not carry on business or establish or keep a place of business in Singapore` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 241(2) the foreign company must not carry on business or establish or keep a place of business in Singapore` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- no order made
#ASSERT `s 241(2) the foreign company must not carry on business or establish or keep a place of business in Singapore` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- not a foreign company
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 241(2) the foreign company must not carry on business or establish or keep a place of business in Singapore once the order is made` "Zed Corp" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a foreign company` "Zed Corp" DOES `s 241(2) carry on business or establish or keep a place of business in Singapore` AT 12
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 241(2) the foreign company must not carry on business or establish or keep a place of business in Singapore once the order is made` "Zed Corp" AT 0 WITH

§ `Section 242`

-- (1): intent, and (a) destroying, concealing or altering or (b) sending or attempting or conspiring to send out of Singapore. Arguments: intent; (a); (b).
#ASSERT `s 242(1) the person is guilty of the offence of defeating the purposes of Part 9 or obstructing an investigation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 242(1) the person is guilty of the offence of defeating the purposes of Part 9 or obstructing an investigation` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 242(1) the person is guilty of the offence of defeating the purposes of Part 9 or obstructing an investigation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 242(1) the person is guilty of the offence of defeating the purposes of Part 9 or obstructing an investigation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- intent but no act
#ASSERT `s 242(1) the person is guilty of the offence of defeating the purposes of Part 9 or obstructing an investigation` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- the act but no intent
#ASSERT `s 242(1) the person is guilty of the offence of defeating the purposes of Part 9 or obstructing an investigation` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years": 24 months, and "or" is not "both".
#ASSERT `s 242(1) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 10000, 24, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 242(1) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 10000, 24, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 242(1) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 242(1)(a) a person must not destroy, conceal or alter a book, document or record of a declared company with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a person` "A. Tan" DOES `s 242(1) destroy, conceal or alter a book, document or record of or relating to a declared company with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9` AT 5
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 242(1)(a) a person must not destroy, conceal or alter a book, document or record of a declared company with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 242(1)(b) a person must not send a book, document, record or property of a declared company out of Singapore with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a person` "A. Tan" DOES `s 242(1) send out of Singapore a book, document, record or property of a declared company with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9` AT 5
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 242(1)(b) a person must not send a book, document, record or property of a declared company out of Singapore with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH
-- (2): the onus.
#ASSERT `s 242(2) the person bears the onus of proving that the person did not act with the intent` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 242(2) the person bears the onus of proving that the person did not act with the intent` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
